.TH crblockmap "1" "" "The scalpel3 Blockmap Creator" "The scalpel3 Blockmap Creator"

.SH NAME
crblockmap \- Create a new scalpel3 blockmap

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crblockmap
[\fB-j\fR \fIstartblock\fR]
[\fB-k\fR \fIendblock\fR]
[\fB-q\fR \fIclustersize\fR]
img_filename
blockmap_filename

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBcrblockmap\fR creates a blockmap for an image file and block size,
initially with no explicitly covered blocks. It records duplicate and zero
blocks during creation. The image must be nonempty and is not modified.
.PP
If a carve window is specified via \fB-j\fR and \fB-k\fR, deduplication and zero block detection occur only within that window. Blocks outside the window are implicitly considered covered by scalpel3.
.PP
Block numbers start at zero and both window endpoints are inclusive. The
start must not exceed the end, and both must lie within the image. A final
short block counts as one block. Options must precede the filenames.

.SH OPTIONS
.PP
.TP
.BI -j " startblock"
Start of the active carve window (default 0).

.TP
.BI -k " endblock"
End of the active carve window (default is the last block of the image).

.TP
.BI -q " clustersize"
Block / cluster size in bytes. Must be a multiple of 512 from 512 through
4294966784. Default is 512. For use with scalpel3 or fragmentator, choose a
block size no larger than their limit of 1073741824 bytes.

.TP
.I img_filename
The source disk image.

.TP
.I blockmap_filename
The filename for the new blockmap. \fBcrblockmap\fR will not overwrite an existing file.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and nonzero on error.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scalpel3 (1),
.BR modblockmap (1),
.BR cmpblockmaps (1),
.BR blockmapfs (1),
.BR fragmentator (1)

